      "prism:coverDate": "1969-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Sept",
      "dc:description": "The Scully Mine, situated in the Labrador Trough near the Quebec-Labrador boundary, is one of the world's largest continuous ore deposits. Paper outlines the sequence of the mining operations from the planning stages to the delivery of the ore to the crusher at an average rate of 50,000 tpd, 7 days/wk. Principal equipment used in surface mining is described. Particular attention is given to grade control, programmed by computer, drilling and blasting techniques and operational aspects inherent with open-pit mining in Canada's north.",
